desc <leader>,t previous tab

" ============================================================================
" Repeat groups — tap-to-continue transient maps
" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
" After any binding whose TARGET is listed in a group below (membership is the
" target, not the key), the next keypress is first looked up in that group: a
" member key re-dispatches its target and keeps the run alive; any other key
" (or ESC) ends the run and keeps its normal meaning — nothing is swallowed,
" and there is no timeout. The entering keypad key needn't be a member. So:
" SPC . e then . . , walks errors; SPC w i then i i i keeps zooming. Syntax:
"   repeat <group> <key> <target>     target grammar = the map-line RHS
"   repeat <group> <key> ignore       give a bundled group's key back
" ============================================================================
repeat error . <action>(org-netbeans-core-actions-JumpNextAction)
repeat error , <action>(org-netbeans-core-actions-JumpPrevAction)
repeat zoom i <action>(zoom-text-in)
repeat zoom = <action>(zoom-text-in)
repeat zoom o <action>(zoom-text-out)
repeat zoom - <action>(zoom-text-out)
repeat tab n <action>(org-netbeans-core-windows-actions-NextTabAction)
repeat tab p <action>(org-netbeans-core-windows-actions-PreviousTabAction)
repeat tab . <action>(org-netbeans-core-windows-actions-NextTabAction)
repeat tab , <action>(org-netbeans-core-windows-actions-PreviousTabAction)
repeat bookmark n <action>(bookmark-next)
repeat bookmark p <action>(bookmark-previous)

" Emacs C-x z: after repeat (SPC x z or '), bare z keeps repeating
repeat replay z repeat
